# --- U_E28  (E28-2G4M27SX, SX1280 + PA, 27 dBm) - WHAT THE BOARD ACTUALLY CARRIES
# ADR-139 (Accepted 2026-10-26) moves this site to a NON-PA LoRa1280 and states in its own
# status line: "Not yet applied to `hub_board_v10.kicad_pcb`". It has NOT been applied.
# Measured 2026-11-11: the board carries `U_E28` and no `U_LORA1280`; the two experimental
# boards (`hub_board_v10_lora1280_swap`, `_7of9`) carry `U_LORA1280`.
#
# SO THIS BLOCK IS THE BOARD, NOT THE RECOMMENDATION. The registry previously described
# U_LORA1280, i.e. the ADR-139 end state, which is why `registry.py check` reported the board
# as drifted. Recording the intended part in the source-of-truth registry makes the registry
# a statement of intent that silently contradicts the copper -- and any tool trusting it would
# validate pins against a part that is not fitted. When the swap IS applied, regenerate from
# the board and this block becomes U_LORA1280 again.
U_E28.1  +3V3  # v9 netlist (rails)
U_E28.2  GND  # v9 netlist (rails)
U_E28.3  /SPI1_MISO  # ADR-123 (2.4GHz bus: U3+U_C+E28)
U_E28.4  /SPI1_MOSI  # ADR-123 (2.4GHz bus: U3+U_C+E28)
U_E28.5  /SPI1_SCK  # ADR-123 (2.4GHz bus: U3+U_C+E28)
U_E28.6  /E28_CS_N  # ADR-118 + E28 sidecar pin map
U_E28.7  GND  # v9 netlist (rails)
U_E28.8  UNASSIGNED  # SEE connectivity/OPEN-ITEMS.md
U_E28.9  UNASSIGNED  # SEE connectivity/OPEN-ITEMS.md
U_E28.10  GND  # v9 netlist (rails)
